NUM-41: give RDII the rain that fell in each time step, not a point sample

getRainfall() took the gage's intensity at the start of each UH rain interval
(one gage_setState() call per RDII time step) and multiplied it by the
interval length. When WET_STEP does not divide the gage's recording interval,
or a UH limb shorter than WET_STEP makes the interval shorter than the step,
that is not the depth that fell, and RDII gets 0.67 to 1.20 times the right
rain. The new getGageRainfall() walks the gage's rainfall changes over each
RDII time step and returns their time-weighted average. Each rain interval
gets that average times the part of the step it covers (from the end of the
previous interval to its own end, at most the current date), so the depths
of a step add up to the rain that fell in it. Where one rain value covers the
whole step the result is bit-identical to before.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-41_swmm530.patch

